      "writtenOn": "2021-03-11T21:40:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is going to be used externally, it should be declared in a header file (probably usb_pd.h). If it is not, it should be declared static here. Either way, it should have a comment explaining what it does.\n\nAs written, it appears to be very specific to its call sites, i.e. it assumes that the cable discovery response is Rev 3.0 (perhaps without consequence, since the 3.0 field is a superset of the 2.0 field), and it does not meaningfully support active cables. As such, it is hard to imagine using this more generally. I would prefer that it have semantics where it just gets the field and allows the caller to do with it what it will, with checks appropriate to the call site.\n\nAs discussed elsewhere, we don\u0027t typically start function names with verbs.",
      "revId": "e19f211c212478e883d94c0a75dd67ca5dfeb222",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
