      "writtenOn": "2021-03-11T21:40:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this function is defined in terms of board_get_max_tbt_speed, it wouldn\u0027t make sense for boards to override it, and it\u0027s not currently overrideable, so I don\u0027t think the name should start with \"board_\". As I described in a previous CL, it is also not the convention of this codebase to start names with \"get_\". I\u0027m not immediately sure what the best name for this would be.\n\nAs I note below, this is called twice, but it only needs to be called once. I recommend combining the call sites, explicitly calling the composition of functions below, getting rid of this definition, and avoiding the issue.",
      "revId": "e19f211c212478e883d94c0a75dd67ca5dfeb222",
